//? Title: Simplex: actual pivots and explicit stopping conditions
//? Subtitle: Actual canonical histories, retained original fixtures and explicit controls
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
A linear objective must be maximized over nonnegative variables constrained by
linear inequalities. With nonnegative right-hand sides, slack variables provide
an initial feasible basis for primal simplex. We trace actual pivots, retain the
original two-variable resource allocation, and explicitly distinguish optimal,
unbounded and iteration-limited outcomes.
)

\toc

> Mechanism and mathematical scope

For maximize c dot x with A x<=b and x>=0, introduce nonnegative slacks z so
Ax+z=b. The origin with z=b is a feasible starting basis only when b>=0. There
is no PhaseI or general infeasibility solver here.

An improving negative objective-row coefficient enters. For positive
pivot-column coefficients, the minimum RHS/coefficient ratio preserves
nonnegative basic values; exact ratio ties use the smallest basic-variable
index. Normalize the pivot row, eliminate its column elsewhere, and update the
basis. The captured tableau is the actual post-pivot state. In exact arithmetic
Bland's rules prevent cycling; finite tolerance arithmetic is not an exact
certificate.

$$\max 5x+4y:\quad6x+4y\leq24,\quad x+2y\leq6,\quad x,y\geq0.$$
\alttext(The original objective maximizes five x plus four y under the two resource constraints and nonnegative variables.)

The feasible vertices are (0,0),(4,0),(3,1.5),(0,3), with objectives0,20,21,12.
The optimum21 occurs at the intersection(3,1.5). One pivot has tableau-sized
work; the number of pivots can be exponential. Smallest-index choices and
tolerances are explicit rather than an unqualified termination promise.

> A tiny actual producing history

The table and native concept diagram read the same producing execution. Every
block below is a complete editable C++ program.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/simplex_tiny.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
    namespace a = dm::algorithms;
    namespace g = dm::graphics;
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    auto r = a::simplex_trace({1}, {{1}}, {2});
    std::print("| actual entering | leaving variable | pivot | actual basis | actual tableau |\n| ---: | " "---: | ---: | --- | --- |\n");
    for (const auto &s : r.history)
        std::print("| {} | {} | {} | `{}` | `{}` |\n", s.entering, s.leaving,
                   s.pivot, s.basis, s.tableau);
    g::Diagram concept_diagram(48, 1100);
    concept_diagram.node("n0", {0, 0}, "Maximize x subject to 0 <= x <= 2");
    concept_diagram.node("n1", {5, 0}, std::format("{} actual pivot", r.pivots));
    concept_diagram.node("n2", {10, 0},
                         std::format("Objective {}", r.result.value));
    concept_diagram.edge("n0", "n1").edge("n1", "n2");
    concept_diagram.save_svg("build/simplex_tiny.svg");
}
```
