> API and interpretation

Optimal and Unbounded are tolerance-based floating-point conclusions; ill-scaled
constraints need independent residual checks or a certified solver.
IterationLimit retains the current basis and never means optimal. Nonfinite
coefficients, ragged shapes, negative RHS and invalid tolerance fail before
tableau allocation. Default tolerance1e-9, pivot cap100000 and tableau bound one
million cells are explicit. The shaded original region and contour are labelled
analytic references; the red point comes from the actual solve.

Reusable producers, fixtures and histories live in the canonical C++ library.
Captured records own their values and do not come from a separate report replay.
Selected counters and record/scalar policies are specified at their API
boundaries; they are not peak-byte or wall-time budgets. Synthetic structural
inputs are controlled fixtures for these mechanisms.

